<p>
  A <a href="https://github.com/basecamp/lexxy">Lexxy</a> editor synced with
  <a href="https://github.com/jpcamara/lexxy-realtime">lexxy-realtime</a>.
  Lexical stores its content in the Yjs document as nested
  <code>Y.XmlText</code> nodes. The page renders the same
  <code>&lt;yrby-document&gt;</code> wrapper the gem's form helper renders,
  with a signed token for this room's <code>body</code> field as its grant.
  Each room has a <code>Note</code> record, which <code>NoteChannel</code>
  creates when the first person joins. <code>NoteChannel</code> extends the
  gem's <code>LexxyRealtime::DocumentChannel</code> and rejects any other
  token.
</p>
<p>
  After each update, the channel renders the note's whole body to HTML with
  <code>Y::Lexxy</code> and saves it to <code>body</code>, a plain text column.
  yrby's tests check that this HTML matches what a live Lexxy editor produces.
  The panel below loads the column over HTTP, so you can watch the saved HTML
  change as you type.
</p>
